From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 2 AVPs from ETSI TS 183 017
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ETSI TS 183 017 V3.2.1 defines these AVPs in vendor 13019, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  Overbooking-indicator (460): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 7.3.35
  Authorization-Package-Id (461): UTF8String, clause 7.3.37

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
index a48da2b..43d8bc8 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
@@ -233,6 +233,14 @@
 		<enum name="PRIORITY-FOURTEEN" code="14"/>
 		<enum name="PRIORITY-FIFTEEN" code="15"/>
 	</avp>
+	<avp name="Overbooking-indicator" code="460" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="yes" vendor-id="ETSI">
+		<type type-name="Enumerated"/>
+		<enum name="no overbooking mode is required" code="0"/>
+		<enum name="overbooking is mode required" code="1"/>
+	</avp>
+	<avp name="Authorization-Package-Id" code="461" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="yes" vendor-id="ETSI">
+		<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
+	</avp>
 	<avp name="ETSI-Service-Class" code="459" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
 		<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
 	</avp>
